hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1237","Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, H. Abu Musa narrated to us, Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, Mansour, H., and Bundar told us, Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abu Yahya, On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying while sitting. I said: It was narrated that you say: “The prayer of a sitting person About half of the Qaim’s prayer, he said: Yes, but I am not like one of you. This is the wording of the hadith of Abu Musa. Bundar did not say: He said: Yes."
